     <widget class="QWidget" name="tab_edgeSnappingLayouts">
      <attribute name="icon">
       <iconset theme="preferences-desktop-virtual">
        <normaloff>../../../../../../../../.designer/backup</normaloff>../../../../../../../../.designer/backup</iconset>
      </attribute>
      <attribute name="title">
       <string>Edge Snapping Layouts</string>
      </attribute>
      <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="verticalLayout_3">
       <item>
        <widget class="QGroupBox" name="groupBox_edgeSnappingLayouts">
         <property name="title">
          <string>Edge Snapping Layouts Configuration</string>
         </property>
         <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="verticalLayout_7">
          <item>
           <widget class="QLabel" name="label_edgeSnappingLayoutsExplanation">
            <property name="text">
             <string>Configure which layouts should be activated when the cursor approaches different screen edges at different distances. Each zone can have different layouts for different distances (far, medium, close). Use layout names instead of indices to make configurations more readable. Note: The distance thresholds (far=[15,10], medium=[10,5], close=[5,0]) are hardcoded and not configurable.</string>
            </property>
            <property name="wordWrap">
